#!/usr/bin/env bitcpy

[ PC and filler values for syscall stuff ]
[ .00000000 ] 00800000 aaaaaaaa 00000000 aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa

[ constants ]
[ .00100000 ] 00000000
[ .02100000 ] ffffffff
[ .04100000 ] 10000000

[ .06100000 ] c3000000 [ exit syscall number ]
[ .08100000 ] 00200000 [ dumpmem syscall number ]
[ .0a100000 ] aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa

[ arrays that are used to simulate a for(0..20) |i| { ... } loop ]
[ there's also a way to do this without shifting over the entire array, ]
[ but i already wrote it this way, and i don't want to rewrite it now ]
[ .00200000 ] 00102030 40506070 8090a0b0 c0d0e0f0 01112131 41516171 8191a1b1 c1d1e1f1
[ .00300000 ] 00102030 40506070 8090a0b0 c0d0e0f0 01112131 41516171 8191a1b1 c1d1e1f1
[ .00400000 ] ffffffff 00000000
[ .04400000 ] ffffffff 00000000

[ .08400000 ] aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa
[ .00500000 ] aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa
[ .00600000 ] aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa


[ add function: X = X + Y (20 bit) (wraps around on overflow) ]
[ this also supports a carry bit, by setting the bit at .1a700000 before calling ]
[ to call: write return address, X, Y; then jump to call address ]

[ .00700000 ] 0a700000 [ call address ] [ never change this ]
[ .02700000 ] 04e00000 [ return address ]
[ .04700000 ] 733a8e92 [ X ]
[ .06700000 ] 8f30d120 [ Y ]
[ .08700000 ] 00000000 [ i ] [ index, only bottom 5 bits are read ]
[ .0a700000 ] 0000499e [ NCXY bits (N is new, C is carry), N and C lookup table ]
[ .0c700000 ] 06800000 [ address to jump to for loop start ] [ never change this ]
[ .0e700000 ] aaaaaaaa

[ .00800000 ] 00200000 00300000 00100000 [ copy the index array ]
[ .06800000 ] 00400000 04400000 02000000 [ copy the loop mask array ]
[ .0c800000 ] 04400000 80000000 10000000 [ check if loop should keep going ]
[ .02900000 ] 00100000 1a700000 10000000 [ if no, reset the carry bit ]
[ .08900000 ] 02700000 00000000 02000000 [ if no, jump to return address ]
[ .0e900000 ] aaaaaaaa aaaaaaaa
[ .02a00000 ] 00300000 08700000 80000000 [ if yes, set i based on index array ]
[ .08a00000 ] 08700000 0ea00000 50000000 [ set X bit in NCXY ]
[ .0ea00000 ] 04700000 2a700000 10000000 [ set X bit in NCXY ]
[ .04b00000 ] 08700000 0ab00000 50000000 [ set Y bit in NCXY ]
[ .0ab00000 ] 06700000 3a700000 10000000 [ set Y bit in NCXY ]
[ .00c00000 ] 1a700000 16c00000 30000000 [ copy lookup table at CXY to NC ]
[ .06c00000 ] 0b700000 0a700000 20000000 [ copy lookup table at CXY to NC ]
[ .0cc00000 ] 08700000 04d00000 50000000 [ set X bit to N ]
[ .02d00000 ] 0a700000 04700000 10000000 [ set X bit to N ]
[ .08d00000 ] 80300000 00300000 8f000000 [ shift the index array ]
[ .0ed00000 ] 14400000 04400000 12000000 [ shift the loop mask array ]
[ .04e00000 ] 0c700000 00000000 02000000 [ jump to start of loop ]

[ code to run after the addition function finishes ]
[ this code is only ran because the return address is initialized to go here, ]
[ but in a larger code base, you would always set the return address before calling add ]

[ .0ae00000 ] 08100000 02000000 02000000 [ dump memory to stderr ]
[ .00f00000 ] 06100000 02000000 02000000 [ exit ]
